Article 10 No entity or individual under any of the following circumstances may become a shareholder holding more than 5% of the equities of a securities company or an actual controller:
(1) Having been sentenced to a criminal penalty for an intentional crime, and less than three years have elapsed since the completion of the execution of the penalty;
(2) Net assets are less than 50% of the paid-in capital, or contingent liabilities reach 50% of net assets;
(3) Being unable to repay due debts;
(4) Other circumstances determined by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.
Other shareholders of a securities company shall meet the relevant requirements of the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.

Article 13 A securities company shall obtain the approval of the securities regulatory authority under the State Council for any of the following: increasing its registered capital with a material adjustment in the equity structure, reducing its registered capital, changing its business scope or material clauses in its articles of association, merger or division, establishment, acquisition or dissolution of domestic branches, or establishment, acquisition or equity participation in securities operating institutions outside the territory of China.
For the purpose of the preceding paragraph, "material clauses in the articles of association" mean clauses stipulating the following matters:
(1) The name and domicile of the securities company;
(2) The organizational structure of the securities company and the methods for its establishment, functions, and rules of procedure;
(3) The types, amounts, and internal approval procedures for external investments and external guarantees made by the securities company;
(4) The grounds for dissolution and liquidation methods of the securities company;
(5) Other matters required by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council to be prescribed in the articles of association of the securities company.
For the purpose of the first paragraph of this Article, "branches of a securities company" mean non-legal-person units subordinate to the securities company, such as branch companies and securities business departments engaged in business operations.

Article 16 The securities regulatory authority under the State Council shall review the following applications and make a written decision of approval or disapproval within the following time limits:
(1) For an application to establish a securities company within the territory of China or to establish, acquire, or participate in a securities operating institution outside the territory of China, within six months from the date of acceptance;
(2) For an application to increase registered capital with a material adjustment in the equity structure, reduce registered capital, merger or division, or to request review of the qualifications of shareholders or actual controllers, within three months from the date of acceptance;
(3) For an application to change the business scope or material clauses in the articles of association, or to request review of the qualifications of senior officers, within 45 working days from the date of acceptance;
(4) For an application to establish, acquire, or dissolve a domestic branch, or to suspend business, dissolve, or become bankrupt, within 30 working days from the date of acceptance;
(5) For an application to request review of the qualifications of directors or supervisors, within 20 working days from the date of acceptance.
When examining and approving an application for the establishment of a securities company or its branches, the securities regulatory authority under the State Council shall take into account the needs for the development of the securities market and fair competition.

Article 43 A securities company engaging in proprietary securities trading shall not engage in the following acts:
(1) purchasing securities issued by an issuer that is a controlling shareholder of the securities company or has other material interests with the securities company, in violation of regulations;
(2) entrusting others to buy or sell securities on its behalf, in violation of regulations;
(3) buying or selling securities using inside information or manipulating the securities market;
(4) other acts prohibited by laws, administrative regulations or the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.

Article 46. A securities company engaged in securities asset management business shall not engage in the following acts:
(1) Making a commitment to a client guaranteeing that the principal of its assets shall not be lost or guaranteeing that it shall obtain a minimum return;
(2) Accepting the value of a single entrusted asset of a client that is below the minimum amount prescribed by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council;
(3) Using client assets to conduct unnecessary securities transactions;
(4) Conducting transactions between a securities proprietary account and a securities asset management account or between different securities asset management accounts, without sufficient evidence proving that effective segregation has been achieved according to law;
(5) Other acts prohibited by laws, administrative regulations, or the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.

Article 49. A securities company that engages in margin trading business shall meet the following conditions:
(1) The securities company has a sound governance structure and effective internal control;
(2) The risk control indicators comply with the provisions, and the financial status and compliance status are sound;
(3) It has the professional personnel, technical conditions, funds, and securities required for conducting margin trading business;
(4) It has a complete management system and implementation plan for margin trading business;
(5) Other conditions prescribed by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.

Article 60 Except under the following circumstances, no client's trading settlement funds or entrusted funds shall be used:
(1) The client engages in subscription of securities, settlement of securities transactions, or withdrawal of funds;
(2) The client pays commissions, fees, or taxes related to securities transactions;
(3) Other circumstances provided by law.

Article 67 The securities regulatory authority of the State Council may require the following entities or individuals to provide materials and information related to the operational management and financial condition of a securities company within a specified period:
(1) The securities company and its directors, supervisors, and staff;
(2) The shareholders and actual controller of the securities company;
(3) Any enterprise controlled or actually controlled by the securities company;
(4) The securities company's bank of account, designated commercial bank, asset custodian institution, stock exchange, and securities depository and clearing institution;
(5) Securities service institutions providing services to the securities company.

Article 68 The securities regulatory authority of the State Council shall have the authority to take the following measures to inspect the business activities, financial condition, and operational management of a securities company:
(1) Questioning the directors, supervisors, and staff of the securities company and requiring them to explain matters under inspection;
(2) Entering the office premises or business premises of the securities company for inspection;
(3) Consulting and copying documents and materials related to the matters under inspection, and sealing up documents, materials, and electronic equipment that may be transferred, concealed, or destroyed;
(4) Inspecting the computer information management system of the securities company and copying relevant data.
For the purpose of ascertaining the business situation and financial condition of a securities company, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council may, upon approval by the head of the securities regulatory authority of the State Council, inquire into the bank accounts of the securities company and any enterprise over which the securities company has a controlling or de facto controlling relationship.

Article 70 Where a securities company has an unsound governance structure, imperfect internal control, chaotic operational management, maintains off-book accounts or engages in off-book operations, refuses to implement supervisory decisions, or violates laws or regulations, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council shall order it to make corrections within a specified period and may take the following measures:
(1) Ordering an increase in the frequency of internal compliance inspections and requiring the submission of compliance inspection reports;
(2) Issuing a reprimand to the securities company and its relevant directors, supervisors, senior officers, and persons in charge of domestic branches;
(3) Ordering the disciplinary action against the responsible persons and requiring a report on the results;
(4) Ordering the replacement of directors, supervisors, or senior officers, or restricting their rights;
(5) Taking temporary control of the securities company and conducting a comprehensive review;
(6) Ordering the suspension of part or all of the business of the securities company or its domestic branches, and ordering the closure of domestic branches within a specified period.
If a securities company's business is suspended or it is ordered to close its domestic branches within a specified period, it shall properly arrange for clients and handle unsettled business in accordance with the relevant provisions.
If the compliance officer has performed the duties of stopping and reporting the illegal or non-compliant acts of the securities company according to law, they shall be exempted from liability.

Article 77 If a securities company falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall be punished in accordance with Article 198 of the Securities Law:
(1) employing a person who does not have the qualification for a position as the person-in-charge of a domestic branch;
(2) failing to remove the directors, supervisors, senior officers, or persons-in-charge of domestic branches who no longer meet the conditions for the qualification for a position, in accordance with the decision made by the securities regulatory authority of the State Council according to law.

Article 83 If a securities company violates the provisions of these Regulations and falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall be ordered to make corrections, given a warning, have its illegal gains confiscated, and be imposed a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 100,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, its relevant securities business license shall be suspended or revoked. The directly responsible person-in-charge and other directly liable persons shall be given a warning and imposed a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, their qualification for the position or securities practice qualification shall be revoked:
(1) entrusting another unit or individual to conduct client solicitation, client service, or product sales activities in violation of regulations;
(2) providing investment advice to clients, making deterministic judgments on the rise or fall of securities prices or market trends;
(3) entrusting another person to trade in securities on behalf of the client in violation of regulations;
(4) engaging in proprietary securities business or securities asset management business, with the investment scope or investment ratio violating regulations;
(5) engaging in securities asset management business, accepting a single entrusted asset value from one client that is less than the prescribed minimum.

Article 84 If a securities company violates the provisions of these Regulations and falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall be ordered to make corrections, given a warning, have its illegal gains confiscated, and be imposed a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 30,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan shall be imposed. The directly responsible person-in-charge and other directly liable persons shall be given a warning singly or concurrently, and a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, their qualification for the position or securities practice qualification shall be revoked:
(1) failing to conduct an audit of the departing legal representative or senior officer and submit the audit report in accordance with provisions;
(2) jointly investing or cooperatively managing branches with others, or contracting, leasing, or entrusting branches to others for management;
(3) failing to report the proprietary securities accounts or the securities accounts of securities asset management clients to the stock exchange for the record in accordance with provisions;
(4) failing to ascertain the client's identity, property and income status, securities investment experience and risk preference in accordance with the prescribed procedures;
(5) recommending products or services that are not suitable for the client situation as ascertained;
(6) failing to designate a specific person to explain the relevant business rules and contract contents to the client in accordance with provisions, and failing to disclose investment risks to the client in writing;
(7) failing to sign a business contract with the client in accordance with provisions, or failing to include the required essential clauses in the business contract signed with the client;
(8) failing to prepare and deliver statements to clients in accordance with provisions, or failing to establish and effectively implement an information inquiry system in accordance with provisions;
(9) failing to designate a specific department to handle client complaints in accordance with provisions;
(10) failing to set aside a general risk reserve in accordance with provisions;
(11) failing to deposit and manage the client's transaction settlement funds, entrusted funds, and the funds and securities in the client's collateral account in accordance with provisions;
(12) engaging or dismissing an accounting firm without reporting to the securities regulatory authority of the State Council for the record in accordance with provisions, or failing to state the reasons when dismissing an accounting firm.

Article 86 If any of the following circumstances occurs in violation of the provisions of these Regulations, the violator shall be ordered to make corrections, given a warning, have its illegal gains confiscated, and be imposed a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 100,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 600,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the relevant business license shall be revoked. The directly responsible person-in-charge and other directly liable persons shall be given a warning, have their qualification for the position or securities practice qualification revoked, and be imposed a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan:
(1) without approval, entrusting another person or accepting entrustment from another person to hold or manage the equity of a securities company, or subscribing for, acquiring, or actually controlling the equity of a securities company;
(2) a shareholder or actual controller of a securities company forcing, instructing, assisting, or accepting that the securities company uses the assets of securities brokerage clients or securities asset management clients to provide financing or guarantees;
(3) a securities company, asset custodian institution, or securities registration and clearing institution using the client's transaction settlement funds, entrusted funds, and the funds and securities in the client's collateral account in violation of regulations;
(4) an asset custodian institution or securities registration and clearing institution agreeing to or executing an application or instruction to use the entrusted funds and the funds and securities in the client's collateral account in violation of regulations;
(5) an asset custodian institution or securities registration and clearing institution discovering that the entrusted funds and the funds and securities in the client's collateral account have been used illegally but failing to report to the securities regulatory authority of the State Council.

Article 87 If a designated commercial bank falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall be ordered to make corrections, given a warning, have its illegal gains confiscated, and be imposed a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains by the securities regulatory authority of the State Council; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 100,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 600,000 yuan shall be imposed. The directly responsible person-in-charge and other directly liable persons shall be given a warning and imposed a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan:
(1) using the client's transaction settlement funds in violation of regulations;
(2) agreeing to or executing an application or instruction to use the client's transaction settlement funds in violation of regulations;
(3) discovering that the client's transaction settlement funds have been used illegally but failing to report to the securities regulatory authority of the State Council.
If a designated commercial bank commits an act specified in the preceding paragraph and the circumstances are serious, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council, together with the banking regulatory authority of the State Council, shall order it to suspend or terminate the custody business of client's transaction settlement funds; the securities regulatory authority of the State Council may recommend that the banking regulatory authority of the State Council impose punishment according to law on the directly responsible person-in-charge and other directly liable persons.

Article 88 If any of the following circumstances occurs in violation of the provisions of these Regulations, the violator shall be ordered to make corrections, given a warning, and imposed a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; the directly responsible person-in-charge and other directly liable persons shall be given a warning and may be imposed a fine of not more than 30,000 yuan:
(1) a securities company fails to publicly disclose information in accordance with Article 66 of these Regulations, or the publicly disclosed information contains false records, misleading statements, or material omissions;
(2) an enterprise controlled or actually controlled by a securities company, an asset custodian institution, or a securities service institution fails to report or provide relevant information or materials to the securities regulatory authority of the State Council in accordance with provisions, or the reported or provided information or materials contain false records, misleading statements, or material omissions.

Article 89 If any of the following circumstances occurs in violation of the provisions of these Regulations, the violator shall be ordered to make corrections, given a warning, have its illegal gains confiscated, and be imposed a fine equal to the illegal gains; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 30,000 yuan, a fine of not more than 30,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the qualification for the position or securities practice qualification shall be revoked:
(1) the compliance officer fails to report illegal or irregular acts to the securities regulatory authority of the State Council or the relevant self-regulatory organization in accordance with provisions;
(2) a securities broker fails to present the securities broker certificate to the client when conducting business;
(3) a securities broker accepts entrustment from multiple securities companies at the same time to conduct client solicitation, client service, or other activities;
(4) a securities broker accepts entrustment from a client to handle matters such as securities subscription or trading for the client.
